\begin{enumerate}
\item
  \textbf{Question}\\
  Seja \(X\) uma variável aleatória contínua com função de densidade:
  \[f_X(x) = \left\{
      \begin{array}{ll}
      \frac{2x}{\theta^2}, & \mbox{se}\, \ \ 0\leq x \leq \theta; \\ 
      0, & \text{caso contrário}.\\
      \end{array}
      \right. \nonumber\] Qual é a variância de \(X\), se
  \(\theta = 53\)?

  \begin{enumerate}
  \def\labelenumii{(\alph{enumii})}
  \item
    \(156.06\)
  \item
    \(1248.44\)
  \item
    \(1404.50\)
  \item
    \(2652.94\)
  \item
    \(140.45\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  \[\begin{aligned}
  E(X) & = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} x f(x) dx \\
  & = \int_{0}^{\theta} \frac{2x^2}{\theta^2}dx \\
  & = \frac{2}{\theta^2}\int_{0}^{\theta} x^2 dx \\
  & = \frac{2}{\theta^2}\left[\frac{x^3}{3}\right]_{0}^{\theta} \\
  & = \frac{2}{3}\theta = 35.33 .
  \end{aligned}\]

  \[\begin{aligned}
  E(X^2) & = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} x^2 f(x) dx \\
  & = \int_{0}^{\theta} \frac{2x^3}{\theta^2}dx \\
  & = \frac{2}{\theta^2}\int_{0}^{\theta} x^3 dx \\
  & = \frac{2}{\theta^2}\left[\frac{x^4}{4}\right]_{0}^{\theta} \\
  & = \frac{\theta^2}{2} = 1404.5 .
  \end{aligned}\]

  Portanto,
  \[Var(X)=E(X^{2})-\left[E(x)\right]^{2}=\frac{\theta^2}{2} - \frac{4}{9}\theta^2 =156.06.\]

